<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry the Blind</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1111–1196</span> · Also known as Henry IV of Luxembourg, Henry I of Namur</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry the Blind (c. 1111–1196) was Count of Namur and of Luxembourg, ruling a large group of lands in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardennes">Ardennes</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a> valley. Long without an heir, he promised his inheritance to his nephew Baldwin V of Hainaut, but the late birth of his daughter Ermesinde in 1186 led to a dispute: Namur went to Hainaut and Luxembourg eventually to Ermesinde.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-the-blind.jpg" alt="Henry the Blind" width="243" height="236" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Augustin Calmet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Henry_IV,_Count_of_Luxembourg.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
